I1017 10:04:06.321449    3082 input_loop.go:106] HandleUserInput called with text: "The Worker has stopped in step 5 (stopped for approval). This run is condition F: there are no issue files. The Worker's latest chat reply is pasted below between the markers. You may also read the code and data in the Worker workspace (read-only). Then show your review (Part 1) and your draft to the Worker (Part 2) in full in your reply, in the format of Section 4 of MANAGER_BRIEF.md (in condition F, every draft is a chat message), and append \"Manager memo 05\" to memos/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/manager_memo.md as in Section 5. Append only: do not modify or delete any existing text in the memo file. Do not edit any other file.\n\n----- WORKER REPLY (pasted by the human) -----\n### Proposal: Schema 2 ($\\gamma$-Structure) Design and Sign Conventions for $C(n+1)$ (Issue I05-1)\n\n---\n\n### 1. `gb_matrix` Specification ($2 \\times 2n$)\n\nThe inhomogeneous deformation is parametrized by the interactions between the fermionic standard pair ($a_1^+, a_1^-$) and the $n$ bosonic oscillator pairs ($b_j^+, b_j^-$).\n\n- **Matrix Dimensions**: $2 \\times 2n$ ($4n$ parameters total, each of odd parity $p=1$).\n- **Row Labels**: `[\"a_1_p\", \"a_1_m\"]`\n- **Column Labels**: `[\"b_1_p\", \"b_1_m\", ..., \"b_{n}_p\", \"b_{n}_m\"]`\n- **Parameter Names**:\n  $$\\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s} \\longleftrightarrow \\texttt{gb\\_a1}\\{\\sigma\\}\\texttt{\\_b}\\{j\\}\\{s\\} \\quad (\\sigma \\in \\{\\text{p}, \\text{m}\\},\\ j \\in \\{1,\\dots,n\\},\\ s \\in \\{\\text{p}, \\text{m}\\})$$\n  - For $n=1$ ($C(2)$): 4 parameters: `gb_a1p_b1p`, `gb_a1p_b1m`, `gb_a1m_b1p`, `gb_a1m_b1m`.\n  - For $n=2$ ($C(3)$): 8 parameters.\n  - For $n=3$ ($C(4)$): 12 parameters.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Gram Matrix Sign Convention Options for Human Selection\n\nUnder the skew-supersymmetric pre-oscillator form on $V = V_{\\bar{0}} \\oplus V_{\\bar{1}}$:\n$$[u, v\\} = \\begin{cases} (u|v) K & p(u) = p(v) \\\\ (u|v) \\kappa & p(u) \\ne p(v) \\end{cases}$$\nBecause $p(b_j^s) = 0$ and $p(a_1^\\sigma) = 1$, graded skew-symmetry requires:\n$$[a_1^\\sigma, b_j^s] = - [b_j^s, a_1^\\sigma]$$\n\nWe propose two concrete sign conventions for human selection:\n\n#### Option 1: Frappat / Reference Document Standard (Recommended)\nFollowing Eq. (22) of [`docs/math/C_inhomogeneous_definition.md`](file://<home>/notebook/git/thm01-R/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/docs/math/C_inhomogeneous_definition.md):\n$$[b_j^s, a_1^\\sigma] = - \\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s} \\cdot \\kappa \\iff [a_1^\\sigma, b_j^s] = + \\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s} \\cdot \\kappa$$\n- **Pre-oscillator form**: $(b_j^s \\mid a_1^\\sigma) = - \\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s}$, $(a_1^\\sigma \\mid b_j^s) = + \\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s}$.\n- **Rationale**: Exactly reproduces the relation stated in the mathematical reference document.\n\n#### Option 2: Direct Positive Commutator Convention\n$$[b_j^s, a_1^\\sigma] = + \\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s} \\cdot \\kappa \\iff [a_1^\\sigma, b_j^s] = - \\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s} \\cdot \\kappa$$\n- **Pre-oscillator form**: $(b_j^s \\mid a_1^\\sigma) = + \\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s}$, $(a_1^\\sigma \\mid b_j^s) = - \\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s}$.\n- **Rationale**: Simple positive sign on $[b, a]$, differing only by a global sign $\\mathrm{gb} \\mapsto -\\mathrm{gb}$.\n\n---\n\n### 3. $\\gamma$-Computation Method in $\\mathcal{U}(A)$\n\n1. **Algebraic Evaluation**:\n   Each generator $X, Y \\in \\mathfrak{g}$ is represented as an oscillator polynomial in $\\mathcal{U}(A)$. The deformed commutator is evaluated via associative normal-ordering:\n   $$[X, Y\\}_\\gamma = [X, Y\\}_0 + \\kappa \\cdot \\sum_{\\text{param}} \\Omega(X, Y, \\text{param})$$\n   where each $\\Omega(X, Y, \\text{param})$ is degree $\\le 2$ in the oscillators.\n\n2. **Closure in the Adjoint Representation ($\\mathfrak{g} \\pmod K$)**:\n   As specified in `C_inhomogeneous_definition.md`, $C(n+1)$ is realized as a subalgebra of $\\mathcal{U}(A)$ by its adjoint representation, where the even central scalar $K = 1$ acts trivially. Modulo $K$, every $\\Omega(X, Y, \\text{param})$ decomposes uniquely and exactly into the basis of $\\mathfrak{g}$:\n   $$\\Omega(X, Y, \\text{param}) = \\sum_{Z \\in \\text{basis}} \\gamma_{XY}^{Z, \\text{param}} Z \\pmod K$$\n   - Verification test results: **$100\\%$ of deformed brackets close in $\\mathfrak{g} \\pmod K$** across $n=1, 2, 3$:\n     - $n=1$ ($C(2)$): 96 non-zero $\\gamma$-entries.\n     - $n=2$ ($C(3)$): 576 non-zero $\\gamma$-entries.\n     - $n=3$ ($C(4)$): 1,672 non-zero $\\gamma$-entries.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Schema 2 JSON Structure (`C_{n}_gamma.json`)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"5.0\",\n  \"algebra\": { ... },\n  \"central_elements\": { ... },\n  \"deformation_parameters\": {\n    \"gb_matrix\": {\n      \"dimensions\": [2, 2],\n      \"row_labels\": [\"a_1_p\", \"a_1_m\"],\n      \"col_labels\": [\"b_1_p\", \"b_1_m\"],\n      \"parameter_names\": [\n        [\"gb_a1p_b1p\", \"gb_a1p_b1m\"],\n        [\"gb_a1m_b1p\", \"gb_a1m_b1m\"]\n      ],\n      \"parity\": 1,\n      \"exchange_relations\": \"[b_j^s, a_1^sigma] = - gb_{sigma, j, s} * kappa\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"basis\": { ... },\n  \"parity\": { ... },\n  \"gamma_structure_constants\": [\n    {\n      \"X\": \"H_1\",\n      \"Y\": \"E_eps1_del1_pp\",\n      \"Z\": \"E_2del1_p\",\n      \"param\": \"gb_a1m_b1p\",\n      \"coeff\": \"1\",\n      \"sign_rule\": \"graded\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"generated_by\": \"src/C_gamma.py\",\n    \"generation_date\": \"2026-10-17\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Human Approval Required\nPlease confirm whether:\n1. **Option 1 (Reference Document Standard: $[b_j^s, a_1^\\sigma] = - \\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s} \\kappa$)** is approved.\n2. The $\\gamma$-computation method modulo central $K$ and the proposed Schema 2 structure are approved.\n\nUpon your approval, we will implement the production generator script and write the Schema 2 JSON files to `data/`. No Schema 2 files will be written until approval is granted.\n----- END OF WORKER REPLY -----"
